	I don't think you can wish for ki-rin corpses, anyway. They're
As; they don't leave corpses.

	They're probably the best steed you can get... tough, fast
flyers that can heal themselves. They can use some equipment too, but
that's a bug, and I'd consider it cheating to exploit it. They're
non-eaters... which on the one hand means that it's not going to eat a
chameleon corpse and turn into a newt or something, but on the other
hand makes it tricky to keep it tame, especially for a non-knight. Also,
if you're restricted in riding, don't bother. Riding is more hassle than
it's worth if you can't get at least Basic in it. (Wizards are okay
there, IIRC.)

	And be warned that even a blessed figurine has a 1 in 10 chance
of producing a hostile monster, and a hostile ki-rin is a dangerous
thing. If you've gotten as far as the Castle wand, you can probably
handle one, but it won't be an easy fight.

	Personally, I'd probably just get a blessed spellbook of charm
monster and hire the first jabberwock I ran into.

